  "id": "mental-imagery",
  "term": "mental imagery",
  "definition": "Mental imagery is the internal creation and processing of an image-like experience without external sensory input, often involving more than one sense. It also refers to the ability to inspect, maintain, generate, and mentally manipulate different kinds of images.",
